# Read AGENTS.md first

This repository ships an operational manual at the repo root: **`AGENTS.md`**.

Cursor does not auto-load it, so treat this rule as the pointer. Open
`AGENTS.md` and follow it for all work in this repo — it is the authoritative
source of truth for:

- **Non-negotiables** (e.g. everything is TypeScript including configs;
  `@repo/ui` ships raw `.tsx` source with no build step; design tokens are
  imported via relative path; env validation is lazy/factory-based).
- **Commands** (`pnpm dev|lint|check-types|test|build`, always `pnpm`).
- **Architecture map** (apps/{landing,desktop,server} → packages/{ui,db}).
- **Common pitfalls** (Electron `.js` vs `.mjs` outputs, CORS `null` origin,
  migrations must be pushed before deploy, etc.).
- **Verification** — `pnpm lint && pnpm check-types` then
  `pnpm test && pnpm build` must all pass before finishing.

When in doubt, defer to `AGENTS.md` and match the surrounding code's patterns.
